<ArticleLayout slug="running-a-tmall-flagship-content" ctaLabel="Plan the year with us" faq={faq}>
  <p class="standfirst">A Tmall store content calendar is the brand's own plan. The promotion dates move from year to year, consumer guides print the wrong window, and the merchant rules reported in the Chinese press ask a store for scores, deadlines and prices. None of them asks for creative.</p>

  <h2>What goes in a Tmall store content calendar?</h2>

  <p>A Tmall store content calendar pins each promotion to the dates reported for that year, then schedules store banners, listing images, detail-page slices and short video ahead of them. None of five promotion rule sets reported in 2025 and 2026 names a creative asset, so the month-by-month plan below is hubStudio production practice, not a platform list.</p>

  <p>What breaks a plan is the date. It shifts by more than a week from year to year, guides misprint it, and the rules land late. So every date here carries its platform and its year.</p>

  <h2>What are the main Tmall promotions each year?</h2>

  <p>Six events, five of them dated in the twelve months to September 2026. Times are Beijing time. "Not dated" means no usable source dates that year's event.</p>

