    </table>
  </div>

  <p>Festival messaging belongs in store modules, where it comes down when the sale ends. The <a href="/resources/insights/tmall-product-image-requirements">Tmall product image requirements article</a> and the <a href="/resources/insights/tmall-white-background-image-rules">Tmall white-background image rules article</a> carry the counted specs behind those rows.</p>

  <h2>What should a Tmall store refresh checklist cover?</h2>

  <p>Production practice, run before each cycle the store joins.</p>

  <p>- This cycle's rules report for this year, read in full. - Sign-up window and listing deadline noted for this cycle only. - Consumer-guide dates set aside in favor of the reported timetable. - Campaign banners and skin built at the widest published width, then exported down. - Main images free of promotional overlay text. - White-background image unchanged and still compliant. - Detail-page campaign slice swapped, body untouched. - Short video campaign cut exported from the master. - A removal date set for the skin and the campaign slices. - Every size confirmed in your own seller backend on the day of production.</p>

  <p>The <a href="/solutions/platforms/tmall">Tmall platform page</a> covers the store work itself, and the <a href="/solutions/retailers">retailers solutions page</a> covers running a catalog through the year.</p>

  <p>Reviewed 27 September 2026. Check each platform's rules for the current year before planning to any date on this page.</p>

  <h2>Questions about a Tmall store's content year</h2>

  <h3>What are the main Tmall promotions each year?</h3>

  <p>On reported dates from October 2025 to September 2026, five platform-wide sales: Tmall Double 11, Taobao Double 12, the Tmall New Year goods festival, the Tmall March promotion and Tmall 618. The dates move every year. The 2026 New Year goods festival spot sale ran from 4 January to 11 February. No dated platform reporting of the September sale was found.</p>

  <h3>How often should a Tmall store be redecorated?</h3>

  <p>No source found publishes a cadence, a campaign skin specification or a size set for event entry modules, and none of five rule sets reported in 2025 and 2026 mentions decoration. The cadence is a brand decision. In production practice, the store changes for each promotion it joins and once each season, then returns to an always-on layout.</p>

  <h3>What content does a Tmall flagship need each month?</h3>

  <p>No platform publishes a monthly list. In production practice, the months before each promotion carry the work: store banners and a campaign skin, detail-page campaign slices, short video cuts, and main image sets for new products. July and August, when no platform-wide sale was dated, go to the Double 11 shoot and the always-on refresh.</p>

  <h3>How far ahead should Tmall campaign content be ready?</h3>

  <p>No platform rule, government notice or survey found publishes a lead time. The rules arrive late: Tmall's 2025 Double 11 rules became public 21 days before the presale, and its 2026 618 rules 22 days before the opening. For 618 in 2026, presale products had to be listed before the presale warm-up, as reported. So production starts before the rules.</p>

  <h3>What can be reused between Tmall promotions?</h3>

  <p>On the derived analysis here, the white-background image and the core main image set carry across cycles, because no reported rule touches them and promotional overlay text sits on the most published main-image prohibition list. Store banners and the campaign skin are rebuilt each cycle, detail pages keep their body and swap a campaign slice, and short video keeps its master.</p>
